  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Dexamethasone is a corticosteroid used for many conditions, including inflammation, autoimmune disease, several cancers and lymphomas, cerebral and macular edema, Addison's disease, and COVID-19. It is widely used, appears on the WHO essential medicines list, is approved for human and veterinary use, and is authorised in the European Union for indications such as multiple myeloma, uveitis, and COVID-19.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q422252&quot;>Wikidata Q422252</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>dexamethasone</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>A01AC02, C05AA09, D07AB19, D07XB05, D10AA03, H02AB02, R01AD03, S01BA01, S01CB01, S02BA06, S03BA01</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB01234&quot;>DB01234</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/5743&quot;>5743</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:41879&quot;>41879</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q422252&quot;>Q422252</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C22H29FO5</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>392.467 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
